From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_WORKERS=<n> sets how many threads build pipelines

Core patch, after 0260. Off unless the switch is set: unset, 0 or not a number leaves all 15 builders.

A first boot after a shader change compiles on 15 threads, and nothing could limit them. T47's heap reached
3,552 MiB with 763 in use, and the run ended out of memory at 468 s. T48 ended at 125 s with 3,104.

Start with 4. T47's cold burst grew 2,432 MiB. If that scales with the builders, which is a guess, each one
costs about 160 MiB: 4 would peak near 1,800, the plan's line for a warm boot, and 6 near 2,100.

The price is a slower first boot, by an amount not measured. New pipelines in play use the same threads, so
they come later too. One builder is already a supported case (HasBrokenParallelShaderCompiling), so no job
waits on a second one.

The log says "Pipeline builders: 4 of 15". The port copies this file to vk_pipeline_cache_cost.cpp, and the
switch comes through.

Of the plan's first item this is the builders only. exploitizm's 8b4cdfb897 is a driver change, so it is
lead-mesh-11 in tools/patch-radv-series. The heap class line is in headless/heap_arenas.inc, which this series
doesn't reach, and is left out.

Compiled with the build's flags, syntax only. Not linked, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index a487d75..b16fc43 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -373,6 +373,17 @@ void SurviveBadAlloc(const char* where) {
 size_t GetTotalPipelineWorkers() {
     const size_t max_core_threads =
         std::max<size_t>(static_cast<size_t>(std::thread::hardware_concurrency()), 2ULL) - 1ULL;
+    // EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_WORKERS=<n>: that many builder threads, at most one per core but one. A
+    // first boot after a shader change builds on all of them at once, and each holds its compiler's
+    // memory and its own heap arenas. Unset, 0 or not a number: as many as before.
+    if (const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_WORKERS"); value != nullptr) {
+        const size_t asked = static_cast<size_t>(std::strtoul(value, nullptr, 10));
+        if (asked != 0) {
+            const size_t builders = std::min(asked, max_core_threads);
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Pipeline builders: {} of {}", builders, max_core_threads);
+            return builders;
+        }
+    }
 #ifdef __ANDROID__
     const int configured = AndroidSettings::values.pipeline_worker_count.GetValue();
     const int clamped = std::clamp(configured, 2, 8);
